<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="prose page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE LIST</p>
    <h1>Small computers.<br />Good games.</h1>
    <p>Potato Approved is a deliberately simple catalogue for finding PC games that do not need modern gaming hardware.</p>
    <h2>Two useful categories</h2>
    <p><strong>Potato Approved</strong> is for integrated graphics and very low-end computers. <strong>Fries Approved</strong> is for games that need a dedicated GPU, but can make do with an old or modest one.</p>
    <p>The first entries are demo content. Their hardware and performance notes are clearly marked as placeholders until they can be replaced with verified observations.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
